<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of the Great Zab</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">750</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution">Abbasid Revolution</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zab">Great Zab</a> was fought in January 750 on the Great Zab River in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>, where the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-revolution">Abbasid Revolution</a> defeated the last Umayyad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marwan-ii">Marwan II</a>. Marwan fled to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>, where he was killed. The battle ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a> in the east and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a>.</p></div>
